ode\"\r\n\t\t\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t\t\t},\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nI checked a handful of the ones that don't have enums in their signature, and they seemed fine, although, I didn't check them all. Doing these sort of \"hierarchical moves\" is tricky because our automated checks won't help catch changes to method signatures, so someone needs to check them manually.\r\n\r\nWe could probably improve our automated checks, though? Like, if they took the old `extension_api.json` and tried to look up every method in the new one? Or, even better, actually tried to load them from Godot? I think that's effectively what the Godot Rust CI does :-)\r\n\r\nAnyway, this specific issue could be fixed by registering some compatibility methods (it'll be a little weird, because it'll mean registering the enums again on `EditorFileDialog`, but I think that should work fine) or adding them to `GDExtensionSpecialCompatHashes`\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3606617919/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3606627254","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111212#issuecomment-3606627254","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111212","id":3606627254,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7W-MO2","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-03T12:27:40Z","updated_at":"2025-12-03T12:27:40Z","body":"> so it would be weird if only one of them posed problems.\r\n\r\nThat's why I said \"at least ... possibly more\" :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nGodot_v4.5-stable_linux.x86_64 --headless --dump-extension-api\r\nmv extension_api.json v4.5-stable.json  \r\n\r\ngodot --headless --dump-extension-api\r\nmv extension_api.json commit-7a228b4b9.json\r\n\r\nbat commit-7a228b4b9.json | jq -c '.classes[] | select(.name == \"FileDialog\") | .methods[] | {name, hash}' | sort > FileDialog-commit-7a228b4b9.jsonl\r\nbat v4.5-stable.json | jq -c '.classes[] | select(.name == \"EditorFileDialog\") | .methods[] | {name, hash}' | sort > EditorFileDialog-v4.5-stable.jsonl\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere are the intermediate files:\r\n\r\n- [EditorFileDialog-v4.5-stable.jsonl](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23905723/EditorFileDialog-v4.5-stable.json)\r\n- [FileDialog-commit-7a228b4b9.json](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23905736/FileDialog-commit-7a228b4b9.json)\r\n\r\nResult of `difft EditorFileDialog-v4.5-stable.jsonl FileDialog-commit-7a228b4b9.jsonl`:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"915\" height=\"919\" alt=\"diff\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd6c0db3-b32e-45da-83ae-7b83a67e0c61\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nSo clearly, some hashes changed. _How_ exactly that happened, I'm not sure.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3606627254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"h